`detectWebGL2` short-circuits on `!window.WebGL2RenderingContext`, so my poster override is correct in principle — the 'full' reading is consistent with the mid-case page reload that also broke the reduced-motion and ring-rendering cases (this repo has concurrent sessions; a Vite full-reload hit my pages). My triage:

- **V2 hidden-advance**: my harness read the time 250 ms *after* restoring visibility, counting legitimate resumed playback. Fix: measure while still hidden.
- **V3 camera deltas**: I compared 400 ms after Return, which includes the designed 0.3°/s rest-orbit drift. Fix: read at the `restoreObserved` frame and keep the strict 1e-6, plus the exact `restoredPoseError` probe.
- **Reloads**: warm each context with one reload after goto.
- **Poster tier**: assert tier only after telemetry exists.
